   424	def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:
   425	    """
   426	    Emit thin rays from single-pixel sources framed by 3x3 walls and merge them angle-dependently.
   427	
   428	    Input structure:
   429	    - The background is the most common color.
   430	    - Each source is a single colored center pixel inside a 3x3 frame of one shared wall color.
   431	    - Every frame has 1-3 missing border cells; each missing cell is a ray seed.
   432	
   433	    Rule:
   434	    - A side gap emits a cardinal ray and a corner gap emits a diagonal ray, always in the outward direction from the center.
   435	    - Rays paint continuously until they leave the grid, hit a non-background input cell, or collide.
   436	    - 90-degree collisions keep the meeting cell painted and redirect to the bisector as one thin straight ray.
   437	    - 45-degree collisions keep the meeting cell painted and continue as one thin zigzag that alternates diagonal then cardinal steps.
   438	
   439	    Key insight:
   440	    - The original width/gap cues are removed, so the only evidence is geometric: all outputs are 1-pixel lines, and collision type is inferred from whether the merged continuation is straight-bisector or zigzag.
   441	    """
